WARNING:CONSIDER_KSTRTO: simple_strtoull is obsolete, use kstrtoull instead
#128: FILE: arch/x86/boot/string.h:27:
+extern unsigned long long simple_strtoull(const char *cp, char **endp,

The simple_strtol(), simple_strtoll(), simple_strtoul(), and
simple_strtoull() functions explicitly ignore overflows, which
may lead to unexpected results in callers.  The respective kstrtol(),
kstrtoll(), kstrtoul(), and kstrtoull() functions tend to be the
correct replacements.

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/deprecated.html#simple-strtol-simple-strtoll-simple-strtoul-simple-strtoull

CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*p)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct ucode_patch)...)
#404: FILE: arch/x86/kernel/cpu/microcode/intel.c:153:
+	p = kzalloc(sizeof(struct ucode_patch), GFP_KERNEL);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

